            {
                "entry_id": "decaaf83-12f2-3f81-b4d4-787b0facc172",
                "word": "masses",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "164c73f2-fb19-33df-a76b-094a5fabc5b0",
                        "entry_id": "decaaf83-12f2-3f81-b4d4-787b0facc172",
                        "glosses": [
                            "People, especially a large number of people; the general population."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04c505d9-45d5-40e6-8ea8-8fa949537bfd",
                                "sense_id": "164c73f2-fb19-33df-a76b-094a5fabc5b0",
                                "text": "The masses were mobilized not only to perform typical activities that are part of agricultural production, but also unusual ones such as killing sparrows and rats that were reportedly competing with humans for food. For instance, in 1958, the people of Tunliu County in Shanxi Province were determined to kill all sparrows and rats within their territory."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89a09ce9-95bc-44b2-b555-02533631e5d4",
                                "sense_id": "164c73f2-fb19-33df-a76b-094a5fabc5b0",
                                "text": "Since first tossing its cartoonish, good-time cock-rock to the masses in the early ’00s, The Darkness has always fallen back on this defense: The band is a joke, but hey, it’s a good joke. With Hot Cakes—the group’s third album, and first since reforming last year—the laughter has died. In its place is the sad wheeze of the last surviving party balloon slowly, listlessly deflating."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b0fc2d9d-6a33-3e52-9c61-06f92b079b04",
                        "entry_id": "decaaf83-12f2-3f81-b4d4-787b0facc172",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The total population."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "30bc81a0-5c2f-4602-aa24-a48ff28d4851",
                                "sense_id": "b0fc2d9d-6a33-3e52-9c61-06f92b079b04",
                                "text": "The masses will be voting this Tuesday."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d49f2080-519d-428f-bbd0-57f094697a98",
                                "sense_id": "b0fc2d9d-6a33-3e52-9c61-06f92b079b04",
                                "text": "Dennis: Listen, strange women lyin' in ponds distributin' swords is no basis for a system of government. Supreme executive power derives from a mandate from the masses, not from some farcical aquatic ceremony."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aa3985d8-9bd4-31fe-9740-9f97f23863ce",
                        "entry_id": "decaaf83-12f2-3f81-b4d4-787b0facc172",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The lower classes or all but the elite."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7257f10f-a49c-47fd-9265-79e5493f19f8",
                                "sense_id": "aa3985d8-9bd4-31fe-9740-9f97f23863ce",
                                "text": "[…] the ignorant masses […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9de69b7-f380-4a26-a1e7-371322ac52bf",
                                "sense_id": "aa3985d8-9bd4-31fe-9740-9f97f23863ce",
                                "text": "Ken Cuccinelli tweaked the famous poem from Emma Lazarus – whose words, “Give me your tired, your poor, your huddled masses yearning to breathe free” are long associated with immigration to the US and the nation’s history as a haven – as part of a case for strict new measures pushed Monday by the Trump administration that could dramatically change the legal immigration system."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bb1f499b-4b1b-4c15-85dd-ce017b383fc2",
                        "source_entry_id": "decaaf83-12f2-3f81-b4d4-787b0facc172",
                        "source_sense_description": "people, especially a large number",
                        "target_lang_word": "masses",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "masses",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2972c237-a726-3bf1-9abe-7d1377040094",
                                        "entry_id": "e494121f-62d0-3119-93c8-80c0b3bb3a85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pluriel de masse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb1a0b64-1edf-48d2-a947-4c784e0ddb28",
                                                "sense_id": "2972c237-a726-3bf1-9abe-7d1377040094",
                                                "text": "Depuis le temps qu'il nous fréquente, nous l’opinion publique, l'ancien nouveau philosophe l'a expérimenté dans sa chair : livrées à elles-mêmes, les masses pensent n’importe comment et votent n’importe quoi. D’où la nécessité de confier la pensée à un vrai professionnel comme lui."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "449a0177-c35a-4229-b61c-e104967b8637",
                                                "sense_id": "2972c237-a726-3bf1-9abe-7d1377040094",
                                                "text": "L'histoire, n'en déplaise aux élitistes et aux complotistes, faces complémentaires d'une même incompréhension, est faite par les masses, aisées, pauvres ou médiocres."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
